Um, I had written a song, my God, when I was 15, where I played the piano and sang this song.

1192
00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:29.120
It was for my GCSE music, which is, I don't know, whatever exams you take here when you're 16.

1193
00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:34.460
And, um, I got an A for my music.

1194
00:50:34.640 --> 00:50:35.740
It's the only thing I ever got an A in.

1195
00:50:35.740 --> 00:50:48.320
And it was so bad because it was also kind of good, but it was a really cheery ditty that I was like, da, da, da, da, da, da.

1196
00:50:48.560 --> 00:50:53.000
And yet it was about the most horrific things, paedophiles.

1197
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:53.700
Oh no.

1198
00:50:53.960 --> 00:51:03.440
And, and I'm not religious at all, but in the, in the chorus, it would be like, at the end of the worry and terror, there's heaven not far away.

1199
00:51:03.940 --> 00:51:08.640
And I remember telling Ricky and Steve this, and they were like, we have to have this in our show.

1200
00:51:09.320 --> 00:51:13.760
And they worked their asses off in season two to try and get it in.

1201
00:51:14.020 --> 00:51:17.040
I couldn't, couldn't find a way to legitimately get it in.

1202
00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:18.880
It was so bad.

1203
00:51:19.060 --> 00:51:21.400
And it was so good because it was so bad.

1204
00:51:21.580 --> 00:51:22.800
It was crap plastic.

1205
00:51:23.240 --> 00:51:29.240
This was, I feel like this story is why you were destined to be cast on this show.

1206
00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:32.700
Because your senses of humor were so aligned.

1207
00:51:33.160 --> 00:51:41.860
This idea of like a song about all the things you kind of aren't supposed to say or discuss.

1208
00:51:42.100 --> 00:51:42.280
Yeah.

1209
00:51:42.400 --> 00:51:43.240
In a peppy manner.

1210
00:51:43.540 --> 00:51:44.620
In like a peppy show tune.

1211
00:51:44.640 --> 00:51:46.140
Never entered my head at 15.

1212
00:51:46.400 --> 00:51:49.780
It was like a peppy show tune that could have opened a sitcom.

1213
00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:50.520
Yes.

1214
00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:51.300
And.

1215
00:51:51.500 --> 00:51:52.860
About the darkest stuff.

1216
00:51:53.040 --> 00:51:53.260
Yeah.

1217
00:51:53.420 --> 00:51:54.440
About the darkest stuff.

1218
00:51:54.440 --> 00:51:56.360
Not, not religious at all.

1219
00:51:56.920 --> 00:52:01.900
And I went, Isaiah and Micah prophesied a friendly world of peace.

1220
00:52:02.400 --> 00:52:02.700
What?

1221
00:52:03.480 --> 00:52:04.080
Did they?

1222
00:52:04.380 --> 00:52:05.300
I have no idea.

1223
00:52:05.480 --> 00:52:06.200
But you got an A.

1224
00:52:06.440 --> 00:52:07.280
I got an A.

1225
00:52:07.340 --> 00:52:07.960
You got an A.

1226
00:52:08.180 --> 00:52:09.400
So bar was low.

1227
00:52:12.020 --> 00:52:14.780
They might have just been in shock, didn't know what to make of it.

1228
00:52:14.820 --> 00:52:16.820
I think it was like, poor girl.

1229
00:52:17.020 --> 00:52:18.700
She's going nowhere in life.

1230
00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:19.540
Let's give us something.

1231
00:52:21.500 --> 00:52:22.580
All right.

1232
00:52:22.680 --> 00:52:24.220
There's going to be a conference room meeting.

1233
00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:27.140
We have to discuss conference room scenes with you.

1234
00:52:27.400 --> 00:52:32.960
David Brent is going to discuss these rumors of downsizing.

1235
00:52:34.280 --> 00:52:36.780
How was this to shoot?

1236
00:52:37.140 --> 00:52:37.440
Okay.

1237
00:52:38.820 --> 00:52:42.300
Probably very like your conference scenes, which they take a long time.

1238
00:52:42.480 --> 00:52:42.600
Yeah.

1239
00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:47.020
And at first you are genuinely trying to like be professional.

1240
00:52:47.400 --> 00:52:48.660
Let's get it done, guys.

1241
00:52:48.820 --> 00:52:49.160
Come on.

1242
00:52:49.160 --> 00:52:49.800
Do you know what I mean?

1243
00:52:50.080 --> 00:52:50.780
This is fine.

