And I was like, oh, this is a great way of getting like a massage.

1356
00:57:06.780 --> 00:57:07.000
Yeah.

1357
00:57:07.200 --> 00:57:08.820
Just telling him to do it in a scene.

1358
00:57:09.720 --> 00:57:15.340
But yeah, a lot of our scenes like that were improvised.

1359
00:57:15.540 --> 00:57:16.420
Just play together.

1360
00:57:16.880 --> 00:57:20.260
Martin really helped me in those because I wasn't as confident then.

1361
00:57:20.260 --> 00:57:23.360
Um, now I'd love to do things like that.

1362
00:57:23.400 --> 00:57:28.080
And I've done a lot of improv at, um, groundlings, UCB.

1363
00:57:28.140 --> 00:57:28.440
UCB.

1364
00:57:28.560 --> 00:57:28.820
Yeah.

1365
00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:31.480
But I used, I was much more nervous of it then.

1366
00:57:31.960 --> 00:57:35.920
And, um, and Martin was just great chatting, chatting away.

1367
00:57:35.920 --> 00:57:40.000
So I really, I relied on him and I'm grateful to him for that.

1368
00:57:40.180 --> 00:57:40.280
Yeah.

1369
00:57:40.620 --> 00:57:44.420
Did you guys have to do like chemistry reads as part of your audition process?

1370
