But Ricky always said people come for the comedy, but stay for the story.

1387
00:58:18.240 --> 00:58:20.920
And I think that's probably good in any comedy show.

1388
00:58:21.260 --> 00:58:25.320
I mean, you guys have so many great stories playing out your relationship with Dwight.

1389
00:58:26.140 --> 00:58:29.800
And you, you remember that The Office is funny and you come for that and you laugh

1390
00:58:29.800 --> 00:58:35.440
your head off, but you see all of these stories with characters you love play out and have

1391
00:58:35.440 --> 00:58:37.680
time and have lengths of time to do it.

1392
00:58:37.980 --> 00:58:40.000
And it's why you keep coming back, I think.

1393
00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:41.920
Yeah, for sure.

1394
00:58:41.920 --> 00:58:45.140
That's, for me, I'm like, what is the heart of the show?

1395
00:58:45.260 --> 00:58:47.240
It's the people and the connections they make.

1396
00:58:47.420 --> 00:58:47.540
Yeah.

1397
00:58:47.740 --> 00:58:47.860
Yeah.

1398
00:58:48.280 --> 00:58:51.540
Well, unfortunately, Don's fiance, Lee, is going to arrive.

1399
00:58:51.820 --> 00:58:52.860
This is a big shock.

1400
00:58:53.080 --> 00:58:54.380
We're not expecting it.

1401
00:58:54.560 --> 00:58:54.680
No.

1402
00:58:54.920 --> 00:58:58.500
Lee with his giant garbage bag box thing.

1403
00:58:58.500 --> 00:58:58.720
Box thing.

1404
00:58:59.120 --> 00:58:59.480
Yes.

1405
00:58:59.800 --> 00:59:02.880
Because Tim was just suggesting that y'all go out and get drinks.

1406
00:59:02.880 --> 00:59:08.480
And so all of our hearts are swooning, of course, but, but no.

1407
00:59:09.220 --> 00:59:12.180
And then they have that awkward, awkward silence.

1408
00:59:12.660 --> 00:59:13.960
Oh, it's so good.

1409
00:59:14.120 --> 00:59:18.580
And then, and then Tim says, what's in the, and he goes up, just tell her I'll be outside.

1410
00:59:19.660 --> 00:59:20.880
It's so awkward.

1411
00:59:21.180 --> 00:59:22.300
He's like, I'm not going to talk to you, man.

1412
00:59:22.300 --> 00:59:27.140
And I love that they never made the character of Lee a bad person.

1413
00:59:27.300 --> 00:59:28.300
He was never a baddie.

1414
00:59:28.880 --> 00:59:32.960
You know, part of you might think, well, maybe he beats her or, you know, maybe he's cheated on her.

1415
00:59:33.020 --> 00:59:36.260
No, he's just not someone you want her to be with.

1416
00:59:36.440 --> 00:59:37.420
He's not her person.

1417
00:59:37.600 --> 00:59:38.300
He's not her person.

1418
00:59:38.440 --> 00:59:38.660
Yeah.

1419
00:59:38.660 --> 00:59:44.560
And, um, you could call him things like a loser and blah, blah, blah, blah, but he's not, he's, he's decent enough.

1420
00:59:44.920 --> 00:59:45.240
Yeah.

1421
00:59:45.620 --> 00:59:56.680
Um, but it's a, one of those things where so many people settle because maybe they're looking for marriage and some, some kind of continuity or consistency and, and they settle.

1422
00:59:56.940 --> 01:00:02.160
And that's what Dawn has done for all of her life until the very end.

1423
01:00:02.480 --> 01:00:04.760
You know, she didn't pursue her dream with the drawing.

1424
01:00:04.760 --> 01:00:11.400
And she didn't pursue Tim and, um, and she stayed with this guy just because it was easier to stay than go, I think.

1425
01:00:11.680 --> 01:00:11.940
Yeah.

1426
01:00:12.260 --> 01:00:13.600
And how many, I mean, I've done it before.

1427
01:00:14.060 --> 01:00:14.260
Yeah.

1428
01:00:14.340 --> 01:00:14.780
Yeah.

1429
01:00:15.460 --> 01:00:15.720
No.

1430
01:00:15.900 --> 01:00:21.040
And I, I do like that Lee's not a bad guy and I liked that Roy wasn't a bad guy.

1431
01:00:21.160 --> 01:00:28.100
And one of the things I did love, of course, we had many more seasons and time to show the storyline than you guys did.

1432
01:00:28.260 --> 01:00:30.820
But I love that Roy found his person.

1433
01:00:30.840 --> 01:00:31.160
Yeah.

1434
01:00:31.400 --> 01:00:31.660
Right.

1435
01:00:31.860 --> 01:00:32.040
Yeah.

1436
01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:35.840
And learned how to play the piano for her at her wedding.

1437
01:00:36.340 --> 01:00:36.480
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1438
01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:43.060
I mean, it just goes to show that he was meant to be happier too, just the way that Pam was.

1439
01:00:43.240 --> 01:00:47.120
And, but yeah, so I did like that they didn't make him like sort of this villain person.

1440
01:00:47.640 --> 01:00:47.720
Yeah.

1441
01:00:47.860 --> 01:00:49.000
He just wasn't her person.

1442
01:00:49.080 --> 01:00:49.260
Yeah.

1443
01:00:49.440 --> 01:00:50.760
He just wasn't her person.

1444
01:00:50.760 --> 01:00:52.520
And he wasn't a bad person.

1445
01:00:52.520 --> 01:00:55.680
You just looked at him and knew, please don't end up with him.

1446
01:00:55.880 --> 01:00:56.100
Right.

1447
01:00:56.100 --> 01:00:59.280
Please don't because he's just going nowhere.

1448
01:00:59.300 --> 01:01:03.960
And he doesn't have any, he doesn't encourage her in any kind of dreams whatsoever.

1449
01:01:04.440 --> 01:01:04.600
Yeah.

1450
01:01:04.760 --> 01:01:06.560
He doesn't have dreams for himself.

1451
01:01:07.080 --> 01:01:09.300
And I think that's a shame for anyone.

1452
01:01:09.300 --> 01:01:13.600
Well, she lights up around Tim and her light goes out around Lee.

1453
01:01:13.780 --> 01:01:14.000
Yeah.

1454
01:01:14.120 --> 01:01:17.560
Like, you know, and you just see it in how you played the character.

1455
01:01:17.560 --> 01:01:23.660
And when I talk about stealing things from you, that was like something that I really

1456
01:01:23.660 --> 01:01:25.840
noticed in your performance.

1457
01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:26.340
Wow.

1458
01:01:26.540 --> 01:01:29.560
And I thought, okay, yes, I like this.

1459
01:01:29.720 --> 01:01:34.960
I like this way that you have different body language around these two different people.

1460
01:01:35.360 --> 01:01:35.800
Right, right.

1461
01:01:35.920 --> 01:01:37.240
And so, yeah.

1462
01:01:37.440 --> 01:01:37.740
Yeah.

1463
01:01:38.020 --> 01:01:43.480
I remember doing the scene at the end of the Christmas specials where Dawn goes home in

1464
01:01:43.480 --> 01:01:44.620
the taxi with Lee.

1465
01:01:44.640 --> 01:01:44.860
Yes.

1466
01:01:45.060 --> 01:01:45.280
Yeah.

1467
01:01:45.280 --> 01:01:46.560
And then she opens.

1468
01:01:46.560 --> 01:01:48.220
Oh, it's giving me chills just thinking about it.

1469
01:01:48.260 --> 01:01:49.280
Oh, she opens the paints.

1470
01:01:49.500 --> 01:01:49.800
Yes.

1471
01:01:49.940 --> 01:01:50.600
She's never give up.

1472
