1511
01:03:27.980 --> 01:03:31.860
And I'm like, aren't we desensitized to it?

1512
01:03:32.100 --> 01:03:35.420
And I remember her in Love Actually.

1513
01:03:35.760 --> 01:03:36.520
I don't know if you've seen it.

1514
01:03:36.700 --> 01:03:37.800
I love Love Actually.

1515
01:03:37.820 --> 01:03:39.500
You're speaking Angela's language.

1516
01:03:39.520 --> 01:03:43.980
That scene with Joni Mitchell and she opens it up.

1517
01:03:43.980 --> 01:03:45.680
She thinks it's going to be the necklace.

1518
01:03:46.000 --> 01:03:52.720
And then she makes the bed and it has this resolve that she's going to go and go to the kids' Christmas play.

1519
01:03:52.920 --> 01:03:54.900
But her dignified crying.

1520
01:03:55.260 --> 01:03:56.560
Oh, so good.

1521
01:03:56.920 --> 01:04:04.700
I have to say, just her story with Alan Rickman in that movie alone was worth watching it for.

1522
01:04:04.800 --> 01:04:05.640
Oh, my goodness.

1523
01:04:05.640 --> 01:04:07.500
And I was like, yeah, you aren't you crying?

1524
01:04:07.740 --> 01:04:08.040
Yeah.

1525
01:04:08.340 --> 01:04:08.620
Mm-hmm.

1526
01:04:09.120 --> 01:04:09.420
Oh.

1527
01:04:10.540 --> 01:04:11.000
Yes.

1528
01:04:11.000 --> 01:04:16.500
Well, listen, I want you to come back and I want us to do the Christmas episode.

1529
01:04:16.640 --> 01:04:17.860
Oh, let's do that.

1530
01:04:18.100 --> 01:04:19.220
Wouldn't that be so great?

1531
01:04:19.460 --> 01:04:19.620
Yes, let's do that.

1532
01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:20.880
Because now I want to watch it again.

1533
01:04:21.060 --> 01:04:22.660
We're talking about it and I want to watch it again.

1534
01:04:22.660 --> 01:04:26.760
And also, by that time, I've got things that I can certainly bring you guys.

1535
01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:28.240
You can't show it on here.

1536
01:04:28.360 --> 01:04:32.240
Because I went to look, but I don't have the pilot script.

1537
01:04:32.240 --> 01:04:35.140
But I do have some scripts still from the show.

1538
01:04:35.460 --> 01:04:35.900
Wow.

1539
01:04:36.080 --> 01:04:37.220
And some really cool photos.

1540
01:04:37.300 --> 01:04:42.160
Because we didn't then have, I didn't, but we didn't have cell phones where you could take a million photos.

1541
01:04:42.420 --> 01:04:42.840
No.

1542
01:04:42.900 --> 01:04:43.900
No, we didn't either.

1543
01:04:44.080 --> 01:04:44.300
No.

1544
01:04:44.500 --> 01:04:47.080
So I do have some really cool pictures and stuff.

1545
01:04:47.320 --> 01:04:48.940
Oh, I would love to see those.

1546
01:04:49.300 --> 01:04:49.480
Yeah.

1547
01:04:49.940 --> 01:04:51.680
We'll have to do a Christmas episode.

1548
01:04:51.880 --> 01:04:52.280
Okay.

1549
01:04:52.280 --> 01:04:53.100
Done.

1550
01:04:53.820 --> 01:05:03.700
Well, the episode ends with the David Brent talking head where he's talking about how the most important thing about a company is not, you know, it's not the building.

1551
01:05:03.700 --> 01:05:04.820
It's not the stock.

1552
01:05:05.020 --> 01:05:05.960
It's not the turnover.

1553
01:05:06.280 --> 01:05:08.000
It's the investment and the people.

1554
01:05:08.300 --> 01:05:08.560
Yeah.

1555
01:05:08.640 --> 01:05:11.320
We did a very similar Michael Scott talking head.

1556
01:05:11.460 --> 01:05:11.780
Mm-hmm.

1557
01:05:12.020 --> 01:05:15.120
It has the same sort of joke where he's like, you know.

1558
01:05:15.120 --> 01:05:17.320
Going to be godfather to someone's child.

1559
01:05:17.820 --> 01:05:18.180
Yeah.

1560
01:05:18.340 --> 01:05:19.140
And then fires them.

1561
01:05:19.360 --> 01:05:19.740
Yes.

1562
01:05:19.920 --> 01:05:20.560
It didn't work out.

1563
01:05:20.780 --> 01:05:21.280
It didn't work out.

1564
01:05:21.280 --> 01:05:23.220
Well, that kind of completes the episode.

1565
01:05:23.220 --> 01:05:30.180
But before we go, I have to ask, what has it been like for you to be part of this legacy that is the office?

1566
01:05:30.440 --> 01:05:31.800
People ask us this all the time.

1567
01:05:31.900 --> 01:05:34.620
But I mean, for you, it's like you started it all.

1568
01:05:35.000 --> 01:05:40.680
I think also because we only did the 14 episodes, whereas you guys, how many episodes did you do?

1569
01:05:41.180 --> 01:05:41.620
201.

1570
01:05:42.600 --> 01:05:43.540
Oh, my God.

1571
01:05:44.060 --> 01:05:44.400
Yeah.

1572
01:05:44.700 --> 01:05:45.080
Oh, my God.

1573
01:05:46.460 --> 01:05:47.840
That's where I envy you guys.

1574
01:05:47.840 --> 01:05:52.500
I'd have loved to have done just to have – that have been my life for several years.

1575
01:05:52.620 --> 01:05:52.700
Mm-hmm.

1576
01:05:52.700 --> 01:05:52.880
Mm-hmm.

1577
01:05:54.760 --> 01:06:02.260
So, obviously, to some degree, because we started much before you and we only did 14 episodes, to some degree, it's a blip in the ocean.

1578
01:06:02.820 --> 01:06:06.200
But it isn't because of the impact that it had.

1579
01:06:06.580 --> 01:06:06.760
Yes.

1580
01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:16.320
And I remember the first time we were nominated for awards, it was for the Comedy Awards in England, which are quite big award show and a really fun award show to go to.

1581
01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:21.900
And we were nominated for Best Comedy and Ricky for Best Actor.

1582
01:06:22.280 --> 01:06:23.940
We were like, what?

1583
01:06:24.340 --> 01:06:27.060
We've been nominated for the Comedy Awards?

1584
01:06:27.060 --> 01:06:31.280
And I remember chatting with Ricky on the phone that night when we'd heard.

1585
01:06:31.300 --> 01:06:35.780
And he was like – he said, God, I really hope this will become my cult following.

1586
01:06:35.780 --> 01:06:40.680
I think – like – and he gave – I can't remember what comedy he gave an example of.

1587
01:06:40.960 --> 01:06:46.100
And we were like, wouldn't that be amazing if, like, people actually watched us more and stuff like that.

1588
01:06:46.120 --> 01:06:48.700
So, we just never saw this.

1589
01:06:48.900 --> 01:06:49.240
Yeah.

1590
01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:51.720
And that lasting-ness of it.

1591
01:06:51.860 --> 01:06:52.120
Yeah.

1592
01:06:52.920 --> 01:06:53.660
But, yeah.

1593
01:06:54.300 --> 01:06:57.840
I mean, again, I will know your show more than I will know mine.

1594
01:06:57.980 --> 01:07:01.600
But that's partly because I don't watch myself hardly ever now.

1595
01:07:01.940 --> 01:07:04.220
And I've done things that I've never seen.

1596
01:07:04.220 --> 01:07:07.620
And – but obviously, I've watched all The Office.

1597
01:07:07.860 --> 01:07:09.420
I just don't remember a lot of it.

1598
01:07:09.980 --> 01:07:13.160
And I wrote a little diary through one of the seasons.

1599
01:07:13.660 --> 01:07:14.340
You had a journal?

1600
01:07:14.620 --> 01:07:15.280
A journal.

1601
01:07:15.520 --> 01:07:16.880
And I wasn't a big journal writer.

1602
01:07:17.320 --> 01:07:17.720
Lucy.

1603
01:07:17.920 --> 01:07:18.140
Yeah.

1604
01:07:18.240 --> 01:07:23.020
You know I read from my journal that I kept while we were filming The Office on here.

1605
01:07:23.180 --> 01:07:28.240
They love to make fun of me because I – my journal writing, I write, like, I don't know.

1606
01:07:28.360 --> 01:07:29.100
What would you say?

1607
01:07:29.220 --> 01:07:30.420
A fourth grader?

1608
01:07:30.500 --> 01:07:31.540
Well, we don't know who it's for.

1609
01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:36.980
However, it's like you're writing it to your future self so you don't forget things.

1610
01:07:37.120 --> 01:07:38.220
But with, like –

1611
01:07:38.220 --> 01:07:38.600
A weird –

1612
01:07:38.600 --> 01:07:39.540
It's like you're writing a letter.

1613
01:07:39.540 --> 01:07:42.400
You'll be like, guess what I did today.

1614
01:07:42.560 --> 01:07:43.200
Oh, that's great.

1615
01:07:43.200 --> 01:07:44.320
You'll never guess.

1616
01:07:44.680 --> 01:07:46.060
Rain came by my desk.

1617
01:07:46.140 --> 01:07:46.920
He farted.

1618
01:07:46.940 --> 01:07:49.020
It was so stinky.

1619
01:07:49.340 --> 01:07:49.780
Oh.

1620
01:07:50.340 --> 01:07:52.660
And then I'll say – and then I'll write something like this.

1621
01:07:52.980 --> 01:07:54.180
Story for later.

1622
01:07:54.640 --> 01:07:55.480
Gotta go.

1623
01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:56.280
Story for later.

1624
01:07:56.420 --> 01:07:57.240
Like, to myself.

1625
01:07:57.500 --> 01:07:58.080
To yourself.

1626
01:07:58.400 --> 01:07:59.420
That's what it's like.

1627
01:07:59.420 --> 01:08:01.120
I'm telling myself, like, diaries.

1628
01:08:01.880 --> 01:08:03.680
But anyway, you're going to come back.

1629
01:08:03.800 --> 01:08:06.160
We're going to break down the Christmas episode, and you're bringing your journal.

1630
01:08:06.460 --> 01:08:06.840
Mm-hmm.

1631
01:08:07.660 --> 01:08:08.920
I like this plan.

1632
01:08:09.600 --> 01:08:14.320
Okay, I'll do that after we – I remember I did it for a few jobs, and I remember thinking

1633
01:08:14.320 --> 01:08:19.460
it needs to be written so that if, God forbid, it got into the hands of press or something,

1634
01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:20.600
it's nothing bad.

1635
01:08:20.740 --> 01:08:24.840
It's just my day-to-day or something funny that happened or whatever that is.

1636
01:08:24.960 --> 01:08:25.080
Yeah.

1637
01:08:25.280 --> 01:08:27.400
I can't wait to hear your journal voice.

1638
01:08:27.660 --> 01:08:28.100
Thank you.

1639
01:08:28.100 --> 01:08:31.500
I'm really looking forward to what I'm feeling like.

1640
01:08:31.700 --> 01:08:31.920
Yeah.

1641
01:08:32.340 --> 01:08:34.840
I mean, you are an office lady.

1642
01:08:35.000 --> 01:08:35.440
Mm-hmm.

1643
01:08:35.600 --> 01:08:37.700
You're the original office lady.

1644
01:08:37.860 --> 01:08:38.540
You are.

1645
01:08:38.700 --> 01:08:38.860
Really.

1646
01:08:38.860 --> 01:08:41.840
I can't tell you how excited I was to hear from you.

1647
01:08:41.960 --> 01:08:45.060
And I was like, I wanted to go on this show for ages.

1648
01:08:45.560 --> 01:08:45.720
Yay!

1649
01:08:46.220 --> 01:08:46.280
Yes!

1650
01:08:46.360 --> 01:08:47.500
Oh, my goodness!

1651
01:08:47.880 --> 01:08:48.100
Yes.

1652
01:08:48.500 --> 01:08:50.580
Oh, well, thank you so much.

1653
01:08:50.700 --> 01:08:53.120
I mean, we should tell people how we met.

1654
01:08:53.600 --> 01:08:54.040
Yes.

1655
01:08:54.360 --> 01:08:55.760
You were doing a show.

1656
01:08:55.880 --> 01:08:56.320
A pilot.

1657
01:08:56.600 --> 01:08:57.860
Yes, here in L.A.

1658
01:08:57.860 --> 01:08:58.200
Yeah.

1659
01:08:58.420 --> 01:09:02.940
And my manager had another client on the show, and she said,

1660
01:09:03.020 --> 01:09:05.480
Jenna, you were just cast on the pilot of The Office.

1661
01:09:05.620 --> 01:09:06.200
Oh, my gosh.

1662
01:09:06.240 --> 01:09:09.680
And I think it would be really neat for you to come and meet Lucy Davis,

1663
01:09:09.680 --> 01:09:11.020
who originated the role.

1664
01:09:11.140 --> 01:09:11.940
Oh, my God.

1665
01:09:11.940 --> 01:09:12.660
And I did.

1666
01:09:12.760 --> 01:09:15.760
I came to your set, and I think I watched your taping.

1667
01:09:16.020 --> 01:09:16.220
Yeah.

1668
01:09:16.320 --> 01:09:18.520
That was the Aisha Tyler project, I think.

1669
01:09:18.620 --> 01:09:18.940
Yes.

1670
01:09:19.180 --> 01:09:20.520
Produced by Lisa Kudra.

1671
01:09:21.100 --> 01:09:21.360
Yes.

1672
01:09:21.360 --> 01:09:21.720
Dan Kaczynski.

1673
01:09:21.880 --> 01:09:22.840
Yes, that's right.

1674
01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:26.760
And, I mean, I was so starstruck, I didn't even know what to do.

1675
01:09:26.760 --> 01:09:28.340
You took a picture with me backstage.

1676
01:09:28.640 --> 01:09:31.580
She showed us the picture when she came to set.

1677
01:09:31.700 --> 01:09:32.140
Oh, my God.

1678
01:09:32.140 --> 01:09:34.500
I remember, we were all abuzz that she had met you.

1679
01:09:34.760 --> 01:09:35.820
That I had met you.

1680
01:09:35.940 --> 01:09:37.240
Oh, my gosh.

1681
01:09:37.340 --> 01:09:40.700
And you were so sweet, and you just were so encouraging.

1682
01:09:41.060 --> 01:09:43.300
You said, like, I wish you all the success.

1683
01:09:43.460 --> 01:09:47.480
I mean, everything you were saying at the beginning of this podcast about, like, there's

1684
01:09:47.480 --> 01:09:52.200
room for all of us, and you can be just as big of a success with your version.

1685
01:09:52.200 --> 01:09:56.860
And it just, you know, we were so nervous about doing it, and that really helped.

1686
01:09:57.240 --> 01:09:59.700
As a cast of our office, we were all rooting for you.

1687
01:09:59.940 --> 01:10:00.340
Oh, that's so lovely.

1688
01:10:00.340 --> 01:10:02.740
We just, we were so, no, God, yeah.

1689
01:10:02.900 --> 01:10:06.760
You said that, and that meant so much, and that gave me so much confidence.

1690
01:10:07.260 --> 01:10:08.220
So, thank you.

1691
01:10:08.320 --> 01:10:09.980
I am so happy to be back in touch with you.

1692
01:10:10.060 --> 01:10:10.400
Same.

1693
01:10:10.540 --> 01:10:10.800
Yeah.

1694
01:10:11.120 --> 01:10:11.540
Me too.

1695
01:10:11.840 --> 01:10:13.000
It's lovely to meet you, lady.

1696
01:10:13.400 --> 01:10:18.000
Yes, so lovely to meet you, and I can't wait to meet the journal version of you.

1697
01:10:18.020 --> 01:10:19.620
Oh, my God, yes.

1698
01:10:19.620 --> 01:10:21.660
Lucy, thank you so much for coming by.

1699
01:10:21.800 --> 01:10:22.160
Yes.

1700
01:10:22.400 --> 01:10:23.280
What a wonderful day.

1701
01:10:23.460 --> 01:10:23.860
Thank you.

1702
01:10:24.700 --> 01:10:25.520
Bye, ladies.

1703
01:10:25.780 --> 01:10:27.320
Bye, original lady.

1704
01:10:32.110 --> 01:10:33.430
How lovely was that?

1705
01:10:33.710 --> 01:10:36.190
I mean, I love that I'm back in touch with her.

1706
01:10:36.370 --> 01:10:43.490
We've been texting up a storm again, and it's just, you know, this podcast, we get to reconnect

1707
01:10:43.490 --> 01:10:47.230
sometimes with people, and it just makes me so grateful.

1708
01:10:47.530 --> 01:10:49.290
And I'm so grateful that she came in.

1709
01:10:49.430 --> 01:10:50.210
She was so excited.

1710
01:10:50.210 --> 01:10:53.090
She's just such a wonderful person.

1711
01:10:53.250 --> 01:10:55.990
Like, the minute you're in the room with her, I just was like, when are we hanging out

1712
01:10:55.990 --> 01:10:56.270
again?

1713
01:10:56.430 --> 01:10:56.810
I know.

1714
01:10:57.330 --> 01:10:57.630
All right.

1715
01:10:57.730 --> 01:11:01.470
Well, thank you so much, Lucy, for coming in today, and thank you guys for listening,

1716
01:11:01.530 --> 01:11:02.790
and we'll see you next week.

1717
01:11:02.950 --> 01:11:03.390
See you then.

1718
01:11:03.690 --> 01:11:08.610
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

